# =============================================================================
# Auther — environment variables
# =============================================================================
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in the values from your Supabase
# Cloud DEVELOPMENT project dashboard (Project Settings -> API).
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# .env.local is git-ignored and must NEVER be committed.
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WARNING — how Vite handles these variables
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vite bundles every variable prefixed with VITE_ into the public JavaScript
# that ships to the browser. Anyone can read them in devtools. That is fine for
# the two variables below, and it is the reason the rules exist:
#
#   * ONLY the project URL and the PUBLISHABLE key may carry the VITE_ prefix.
#   * The Supabase SECRET / SERVICE-ROLE key must NEVER appear in this file, in
#     .env.local, in any VITE_ variable, or anywhere in the frontend. It
#     bypasses Row Level Security entirely. It belongs only in Edge Function
#     secrets, in a later milestone.
#   * The publishable key is safe in the browser ONLY because database
#     permissions (GRANTs) and RLS policies refuse to serve data they should
#     not. It is not a security boundary by itself.
#
# See docs/security.md and architecture section E.5.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Your Supabase Cloud DEVELOPMENT project URL.
# Format: https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co

# Your Supabase project's PUBLISHABLE key (previously called the "anon" key).
# This is the public, browser-safe key. NOT the secret / service-role key.
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=your-publishable-key-here
